Free-observation phase is over (3 obs used: Ea→1, Vx→0, Wt→1). Time to move to formal commitments.

**Analysis of the 3×3 pairs (formula = literal_i OP literal_j, OP∈{AND,OR,XOR}):**

- Pair (p1,p2): Wt=(p1=0,p2=0)→1 and Vx=(p1=0,p2=0)→0 — identical inputs, different outputs. No formula over {p1,p2} can explain this. **Eliminated entirely.**
- Pair (p0,p1) and pair (p0,p2) are structurally identical (p1 and p2 have the same values across Ea/Wt/Vx). Checking all sign/OP combos against the 3 observations, only two truth-table-distinct survivors per pair (AND-type formulas all fail):
  - **H1:** (¬p0) XOR p1
  - **H2:** (¬p0) OR p1
  - **H3:** (¬p0) XOR p2
  - **H4:** (¬p0) OR p2

All four remain consistent with all three observations, and I have no basis yet to favor one — uniform prior.

Predictions on remaining symbols (Kr=[0,1,1], Tg=[0,1,0], Um=[1,0,1]):

| | Kr | Tg | Um |
|---|---|---|---|
|H1|0|0|0|
|H2|1|1|0|
|H3|0|1|1|
|H4|1|1|1|

TEST(Kr) splits evenly {H1,H3}=0 vs {H2,H4}=1, and critically, whichever way Kr resolves, a follow-up TEST(Um) will fully separate the remaining pair (0 vs 1 in both cases). This is the most efficient path to full determination.

